## Objective
Implement session persistence to save and restore browser state (cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage) across restarts, reducing login requests and avoiding detection.

## Background
Re-logging in every session creates patterns bot detection systems track. By persisting session state:
- Reduce requests to login pages (stealth via efficiency)
- Appear as returning user (more human)
- Avoid repeated authentication flows
- Maintain session across application restarts

## Acceptance Criteria
✅ Save cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage to disk/Redis
✅ Restore session state on browser launch
✅ Encrypt sensitive session data
✅ Expire old sessions (configurable TTL)
✅ Multi-platform session isolation
✅ Atomic save/restore operations

## Implementation

### Session State Model
```csharp
public class BrowserSession
{
    public string SessionId { get; set; }
    public string Platform { get; set; } // LinkedIn, Indeed, etc
    public List<Cookie> Cookies { get; set; }
    public Dictionary<string, string> LocalStorage { get; set; }
    public Dictionary<string, string> SessionStorage { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public DateTime ExpiresAt { get; set; }
}
```

### Storage Options
1. Redis: Fast, shared across workers
2. Filesystem: Encrypted JSON files
3. PostgreSQL: Durable, queryable

